==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/wɛld/}}
* {{rhymes|ɛld}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|welde|lang=enm}}, {{term|wolde|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|walþō|lang=gem-pro}} (cf. {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|wouw|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|walde|lang=gml}}, {{term|wolde|lang=gml}}, ''[[gaude]]'' in French), from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|walþuz||forest|lang=gem-pro}}. More at {{l|en|wold}}.

====Alternative forms====
* [[wold]]

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[herb]] (''[[Reseda luteola]]'') related to [[mignonette]], growing in Europe, and to some extent in America, used to make a yellow dye; [[dyer's broom]]; [[dyer's rocket]]; [[dyer's weed]]; [[wild woad]].
# The yellow coloring matter or dye extracted from this plant.

